CORE gnu-extensions
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ unsigned one-bit bit-field: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The underlying type of an unscoped enumeration without enum-base was always
int, so (F)-1 was negative, a one-bit bit-field of enumeration type could not
hold the value 1, and a mode(byte) enumeration was a signed char: an array of
size (M)255 had size -1, which failed an invariant in static_lifetime_init.
Integral promotion of such enumerations was always to int.
